   "nrr:openQuestions": [
    "Why did we see no reproducible activity in response to itch?",
    "How could we improve the methodology to enable this measurement?"
   ],
   "nrr:abandonmentReasons": [
    "technical-gap"
   ],
   "nrr:cost": {
    "wetLabRuns": 13,
    "humanExperimenters": 2,
    "note": "13 imaging trials across 5 mice. The pub reports the imaging system cost (approximately US$30,000 including the camera) as capital, not as the cost of this study; no per-study cost is given.",
    "source": "Methods, Microscope and sensory stimulation hardware"
   },
   "nrr:provenanceNotes": [
    "Icebox statement: Our original goal was to employ this technique to complement traditional mouse behavioral assays for itch. Using widefield autofluorescence microscopy, we observed no consistent brain activity in response to histamine-induced itch. We're therefore icing this concept for now.",
    "Mouse identity per trial is not given in the pub. Trials are grouped into animals here from the authors' 'same mouse as in B/C' statements and shared session dates; those groupings are inferred, not stated.",
    "The pub says vehicle trials were imaged for 10 minutes, while the figure legends and the deposited file names say 15 minutes. The trial table follows the file names.",
    "Figure 3D is described as the same mouse as Figure 3C, but its Data IDs carry an earlier session date (2024-03-18) than 3C (2024-03-19). Recorded as printed.",
    "No statistical test, power analysis or detection limit appears anywhere in the pub; effect values are therefore qualitative or single-trial."
   ],
   "nrr:sourceLicense": "CC BY 4.0",
